c**\n(x - 8)(x + 2) = 0\n\nThis gives us: x = 8 or x = -2\n\n**Step 5: Check domain restrictions**\nFor the original equation to be valid:\n- log₂(x) requires x > 0\n- log₂(x - 6) requires x - 6 > 0, so x > 6\n\nOnly x = 8 satisfies both conditions (x > 6).\n\n**Step 6: Verify**\nlog₂(8) + log₂(8 - 6) = log₂(8) + log₂(2) = 3 + 1 = 4 ✓\n\nANSWER: 8","ttft_ms":4423,"type":"result","duration_ms":7236,"uuid":"638e1b5c-519c-43a8-9c7c-b98ecd8cf8a9","ttft_stream_ms":851,"time_to_request_ms":44,"queued_turn_count":0}
